  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lifesaving Assistance to Displaced Populations in the Far-North and South-West Regions of Cameroon through Shelter/Non-food Items (NFI) and Cash for Rent</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the Far North (FN) region of Cameroon, the continuation of hostilities and violence has heavily impacted local populations, where displacement is still triggered by sporadic small-scale attacks carried out by non-state armed groups as well as by seasonal floods, other disasters and intercommunal tensions, creating a great need for capacity building for rapid humanitarian assistance. In the North West and South West regions, the separatist crisis continued to cause massive internal displacement in search of safety and shelter such as bushes or host communities. The ongoing violence also puts additional pressure on vulnerable communities that are already held back, and hard-to-reach communities are particularly vulnerable.The overall objective of this project is to contribute to improving the well-being, dignity and lives of displaced populations through the distribution of emergency shelter and non-food items (NFI). Through this project, IOM is responding to the most urgent and essential needs for unfunded shelter and NFIs for humanitarian assistance to displaced and vulnerable populations in these areas, while easing pressure on host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
